{"parse": {"title": "Boat fishing spot (big net, harpoon)", "pageid": 677016, "revid": 15326821, "redirects": [], "wikitext": {"*": "{{Otheruses|the fishing spot at sea|the spots reachable from land|Fishing spot (big net, harpoon)}}\n{{Infobox NPC\n|name = Fishing spot\n|image = [[File:Boat fishing spot.webp|300px]]\n|release = [[5 August]] [[2026]]\n|update = Wyrmscraig & Sailing Changes\n|members = Yes\n|location = [[Rimmington Strait]]\n|options = Big net, Harpoon\n|examine = I can see fish swimming in the water.\n|map = {{Map|mtype=pin|x=2885|y=3194|zoom=1}}\n|id = 16339\n|size = 5\n}}\nA '''fishing spot''' with [[big net]] and [[harpoon]] options can be found just north of [[Musa Point]]. The spot never moves or despawns. It can only be accessed by sailing to it, and fish can only be caught from a [[raft]]. All raw and cooked fish that can be caught here may be stored in a [[cargo hold]], though the miscellaneous junk from big net fishing can not.\n\nClosest port to bank and unload is west at [[Ardougne|Ardougne port]]. There is a deposit box there, and an assigned crewmate has a dialog option to unload all cargo. \n\n{| class=wikitable\n!Tools\n!Catches\n!Boats\n|-\n|{{plink|Big fishing net}}\n|{{plink|Raw mackerel}}<br>{{plink|Raw cod}}<br>{{plink|Raw bass}}\n|[[Raft]]\n|-\n|{{plink|Harpoon}}\n|{{plink|Raw shark}}\n|[[Raft]]\n|}\n\n==Big net==\n{{Fishing info\n|name = Fishing spot\n|level = 16\n|xp = Varies\n|tool = {{plink|Big fishing net}}\n|bait = Nothing\n|dropversion = Big net\n}}\n\nWhen fishing with a big net, each item is rolled independently, with rarities depending on Fishing level. A roll is made for each item on the table below, save for the raw mackerel, which is rolled twice.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1312360853723844609|date=3 October 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/99298|archivedate=4 October 2020|quote=9 rolls: Boots Seaweed Gloves Mackerel Another mackerel Oyster Casket Cod Bass}} It is hence possible to catch multiple items simultaneously. Additional fish can be caught using [[#Equipment|special equipment]].\n\nMackerel can be caught from level 16 Fishing, granting 20 Fishing XP; cod can be caught from level 23, granting 45 XP, and bass can be caught from level 46, granting 100 XP.\n\nWearing a [[skills necklace]] with at least one charge while big net fishing will slightly increase the chance of finding a [[casket]].{{CiteTwitter|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1574717183888072705|author=Mod Ash|date=27 September 2022|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/99014|archivedate=20 December 2022|quote=Your chance of a casket from big net fishing [while wearing a charged skills necklace] is about 0.4 percentage points higher.}} If multiple types of fish are gained in the same catch, the player will receive a roll to obtain the [[heron]] pet for each type of fish that is caught.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://x.com/JagexAsh/status/1342431578836918272|date=25 December 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27964311|archivedate=5 August 2026|quote=[when big net fishing, if you get multiple fish in 1 catch does it roll for the pet once or for each fish caught?] (...) Anyway, the answer is that you get a pet roll for each fish type caught. (...)}}\n\n{{DropsTableHead|dropversion=Big net}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Raw mackerel|quantity=1|rarity=common|skill=Fishing|level=16}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Raw cod|quantity=1|rarity=common|skill=Fishing|level=23}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Raw bass|quantity=1|rarity=common|skill=Fishing|level=46}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Leather boots|quantity=1|rarity=Uncommon|skill=Fishing|level=16}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Leather gloves|quantity=1|rarity=Uncommon|skill=Fishing|level=16}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Seaweed|quantity=1|rarity=Uncommon|skill=Fishing|level=16}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Oyster|quantity=1|rarity=Uncommon|skill=Fishing|level=16}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Casket|quantity=1|rarity=Rare|skill=Fishing|level=16}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Big bass|quantity=1|rarity=Very rare|skill=Fishing|level=46|Raritynotes={{Refn|There is a 1/1000 chance to catch a [[big bass]] instead of a [[raw bass|normal bass]].{{CiteTwitter|name=bigFishDropRates|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/587574469616476162|date=13 April 2015|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/101775|archivedate=26 March 2019|quote=Bass = 1/1000. Swordfish = 1/2500. Shark = 1/5000.}}|group=d}}|gemw=no}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\nThe chance of successfully catching a fish varies with Fishing level.\n\n{{Skilling success chart|label=Big net fishing chance|showbefore=no\n|label1=Bass|low1=3|high1=40|req1=46|color1=#cb410b|image1=Raw bass.png\n|label2=Cod|low2=4|high2=55|req2=23|color2=blue|image2=Raw cod.png\n|label3=Casket|low3=1|high3=2|req3=16|color3=gold|image3=Casket.png\n|label4=Casket (skills necklace)|low4=2|high4=3|req4=16|color4=purple|image4=Casket.png\n|label5=Oyster|low5=3|high5=7|req5=16|color5=wheat|image5=Oyster.png\n|label6=Mackerel|low6=5|high6=65|bonuslow6=10|bonushigh6=10|req6=16|color6=#efcc00|image6=Raw mackerel.png\n|label7=Leather gloves|low7=5|high7=5|req7=16|color7=saddlebrown|image7=Leather gloves.png\n|label8=Seaweed|low8=10|high8=10|req8=16|color8=green|image8=Seaweed.png\n|label9=Leather boots|low9=10|high9=10|req9=16|color9=tan|image9=Leather boots.png\n}}\n\n===Tertiary===\n{{DropsTableHead|dropversion=Small net}}\n{{SkillingTertiaryDropLines|skill=fishing|varlamore=no|baserate=1147827|minlevel=16|maxlevel=99}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n==Harpoon==\n{{Fishing info\n|name = Fishing spot \n|level = 76\n|xp = 110\n|tool = {{plink|Harpoon}} or {{plink|Barb-tail harpoon}}\n|bait = Nothing\n|dropversion = Harpoon\n}}\n\nThe fishing spot produces one [[shark]] and 110 [[Fishing]] XP on every successful fishing attempt, with a 1/5,000 chance to receive a [[big shark]] instead of a shark. More than one fish can be caught at a time using [[#Equipment|special equipment]].\n\n{{DropsTableHead|dropversion=Harpoon}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Raw shark|quantity=1|rarity=4999/5000|skill=Fishing|level=76}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Big shark|quantity=1|rarity=1/5000|skill=Fishing|level=76|raritynotes={{NamedRef|bigFishDropRates}}|gemw=no}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\nThe chance of successfully catching a fish varies with Fishing level.\n\n{{Skilling success chart|label=Harpoon fishing chance|showbefore=no\n|label1=Regular or barb-tailed|low1=3|high1=40|req1=76|color1=#736b6b|image1=Harpoon.png\n|label2=Dragon|low2=3|high2=48|req2=76|color2=firebrick|image2=Dragon harpoon.png\n|label3=Crystal|low3=4|high3=54|req3=76|color3=cyan|image3=Crystal harpoon.png\n}}\n\n===Shark Lure===\n<tabber>\nHarpoon=\n{{Skilling success chart|label=Shark fishing chance (Harpoon + Shark lures)|showbefore=no\n|label1=No shark lure|low1=3|high1=40|req1=76|color1=#736b6b|image1=Harpoon.png\n|label2=1x shark lure|low2=9|high2=120|req2=76|color2=#736b6b|image2=Harpoon.png\n|label3=3x shark lure|low3=13.5|high3=180|req3=76|color3=#736b6b|image3=Harpoon.png\n|label4=5x shark lure|low4=18|high4=240|req4=76|color4=#736b6b|image4=Harpoon.png\n}}\n|-|\nDragon harpoon=\n{{Skilling success chart|label=Shark fishing chance (Dragon harpoon + Shark lures)|showbefore=no\n|label1=No shark lure|low1=3|high1=48|req1=76|color1=firebrick|image1=Dragon harpoon.png\n|label2=1x shark lure|low2=9|high2=144|req2=76|color2=firebrick|image2=Dragon harpoon.png\n|label3=3x shark lure|low3=13.5|high3=216|req3=76|color3=firebrick|image3=Dragon harpoon.png\n|label4=5x shark lure|low4=18|high4=288|req4=76|color4=firebrick|image4=Dragon harpoon.png\n}}\n|-|\nCrystal harpoon=\n{{Skilling success chart|label=Shark fishing chance (Crystal harpoon + Shark lures)|showbefore=no\n|label1=No shark lure|low1=4|high1=54|req1=76|color1=cyan|image1=Crystal harpoon.png\n|label2=1x shark lure|low2=12|high2=162|req2=76|color2=cyan|image2=Crystal harpoon.png\n|label3=3x shark lure|low3=18|high3=243|req3=76|color3=cyan|image3=Crystal harpoon.png\n|label4=5x shark lure|low4=24|high4=324|req4=76|color4=cyan|image4=Crystal harpoon.png\n}}\n</tabber>\n\n===Tertiary===\n{{DropsTableHead|dropversion=Harpoon}}\n{{SkillingTertiaryDropLines|skill=fishing|varlamore=no|baserate=82243|minlevel=76|maxlevel=99}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n==Equipment==\n*{{plink|Rada's blessing 1}} - 2% chance to catch an extra fish.\n*{{plink|Rada's blessing 2}} - 4% chance to catch an extra fish.\n*{{plink|Rada's blessing 3}} - 6% chance to catch an extra fish.\n*{{plink|Rada's blessing 4}} - 8% chance to catch an extra fish.\n*{{plink|Spirit flakes}} - 50% chance to catch an extra fish.\n*{{plink|Angler's outfit|pic=Angler hat}} - boosts Fishing experience by 2.5%.\n*{{plink|Skills necklace}} - when charged, increases the chance to find a casket when big net fishing.\n\n==Changes==\n{{Subject changes header}}\n{{Subject changes\n|date = 19 August 2026\n|update = Summer Sweep Up - Hunter & Skilling\n|change = The fishing spots where you can fish from your boat now have map icons.\n}}\n{{Subject changes footer}}\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Fishing spots}}"}}, "fetchedAt": "2026-10-06T04:21:44.740130+00:00", "dropHtml": "<table class=\"wikitable sortable filterable item-drops autosort=4,a\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"border-right: none;\" class=\"drops-img-header drop-disp-btn unsortable\" title=\"Sort items by category, rarity and name.\"></th>\n<th style=\"border-left: none;\" class=\"item-col\">Item</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">Quantity</th>\n<th>Rarity</th>\n<th class=\"ge-column\" data-sort-type=\"number\">Price</th>\n<th class=\"alch-column\" data-sort-type=\"number\">High Alch</th>\n</tr>\n\n<tr style=\"text-align:center\"><td class=\"inventory-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/w/Raw_mackerel\" title=\"Raw mackerel\"><img alt=\"Raw mackerel.png: Boat fishing spot (big net, harpoon) drops Raw mackerel with rarity Common in qu